      "papers": [],
      "scope": "Expands activity-log initialization inside processor memory setup. VM log failure, P0 temporary-allocation failure and later sync failure compose with processor rollback. The inner caller releases initialized P0 log buffers before failure handoff; outer rollback owns only VM log resources. VM-only abort leaks buffers; delayed outer cleanup violates error-return ownership even if final cleanup empties resources. Fresh exclusive P0, successful returning destructors and POSIX boolean initializer assumed; disabled logging included. The pstate-log-owned-rollback Fixture binds the proposed owned-memory-ready log cleanup in setup.c. Excludes general VM constructor, concurrent readers, live-slot retirement, semantic C refinement, bootstrap and native admission."
    }
